{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119855","id":3763952640,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7gWVwA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119855","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119855.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119855.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119855","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119855/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119855/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119855/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/336f7aba2647458cf0bafec74783f24097de1926","number":119855,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"🤖 Add Curve2D circle and rectangle builders","user":{"login":"cookesan","id":6601329,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MDEzMjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6601329?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan","html_url":"https://github.com/cookesan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [!INFO] *AI disclosure*: This contribution was authored by an autonomous AI agent, on behalf of cookesan, to add reusable Curve2D circle and rectangle path builders and expose them in the Path2D editor.\n\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\nPath2D is useful with PathFollow2D, but creating common closed paths such as circles and rectangles currently requires manually placing Bezier points or writing the same setup code in each project.\n\nThis adds:\n\n- `Curve2D.create_circle(radius, center = Vector2())`\n- `Curve2D.create_rectangle(rect)`\n- Path2D editor toolbar buttons for creating a default circle or rectangle curve with undo/redo support\n\n## Additional information\n\n`create_circle()` uses the standard four-segment cubic Bezier circle approximation. `create_rectangle()` normalizes negative `Rect2` sizes with `Rect2.abs()` and rejects zero-size rectangles.\n\nThe scope is intentionally limited to reusable Curve2D path construction and Path2D authoring. It does not add a general 2D shape node or drawing primitive system.\n\nValidation performed:\n\n- `python3 misc/scripts/file_format.py scene/resources/curve.h scene/resources/curve.cpp editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.h editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.cpp tests/scene/test_curve_2d.cpp doc/classes/Curve2D.xml`\n- `python3 misc/scripts/copyright_headers.py scene/resources/curve.h scene/resources/curve.cpp editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.h editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.cpp tests/scene/test_curve_2d.cpp`\n- `python3 misc/scripts/header_guards.py scene/resources/curve.h editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.h`\n- `python3 misc/scripts/validate_includes.py scene/resources/curve.cpp editor/scene/2d/path_2d_editor_plugin.cpp tests/scene/test_curve_2d.cpp`\n- `pipx run --spec xmlschema python misc/scripts/validate_xml.py doc/classes/Curve2D.xml`\n- `bin/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64 --doctool --headless`\n- `./misc/scripts/validate_extension_api.sh bin/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64`\n- `pipx run --spec \"scons>=4.8,<5\" scons platform=macos target=editor tests=yes dev_build=yes vulkan=no angle=no accesskit=no -j4`\n- `bin/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64 --headless --test --test-case=\"*[Curve2D]*\"`\n- `bin/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64 --headless --test --test-case=\"*[Path2D]*\"`\n- `bin/godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64 --headless --test --test-case=\"*[PathFollow2D]*\"`","labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":6051509301,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABaLK0NQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/spam","name":"spam","description":"","color":"E94A26","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-05-28T18:13:04Z","updated_at":"2026-05-28T18:37:55Z","closed_at":"2026-05-28T18:17:52Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a46850d2fdfbb1b8d002455717dcb54dccede89d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"cookesan:add-path2d-curve-primitives","ref":"add-path2d-curve-primitives","repo":{"id":1245393745,"node_id":"R_kgDOSjszUQ","name":"godot","full_name":"cookesan/godot","owner":{"login":"cookesan","id":6601329,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MDEzMjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6601329?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan","html_url":"https://github.com/cookesan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cookesan/repos","events_url":"